  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - \r\nThe London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 1 February 2008, the retention of a single storey rear conservatory measuring 4m wide by 4.7m depth by 3.3m high was not lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development exceeds the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the combined extensions exceed 70m3 and inadequate information has been provided to prove the conservatory is more than four years old and immune from Enforcement.  The information provided indicates when the conservatory was purchased but not when it was built.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n"
